idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54302, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01PcNHMBHS4zipN4BqhprXoQ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 58856, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened a SEV2 incident; checkout-api is healthy again.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, was also marked unhealthy. v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release, so I rolled back to it. No approval was needed, since v2.3.0 has been healthy in production before.\n- **Result:** After the rollback, the service reports healthy and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2) is open and has paged on-call. It describes the failure, the rollback and the result, and says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before it's deployed again. My first attempt to create it timed out. The incident list was empty afterwards, so I retried with the same idempotency key, which stops it being created twice.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PBmVYJiTDgGpveV9Wg46u6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012V9hAJogGrpxwJ1v66oYgm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent healthy release is v2.3.0. The list isn't fully in order: v2.3.1-rc has seq 2 and v2.3.1 has seq 3. Both are unhealthy, so either way v2.3.0 is the target.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_016C6ugSDqj6Lhje6sY